#!/bin/sh
# Compact st-reflow help in a temporary floating terminal.

tmp=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/st-reflow-help.XXXXXX") || exit 1

cat > "$tmp" <<'EOF'
st-reflow quick help
====================

Copy / paste
------------
CLIPBOARD workflow:
  1. Select with mouse drag, Alt+drag for a rectangle, or copy mode (`v` regular,
     `V` line-wise, Ctrl+V rectangular). In mouse-aware apps, use Shift+Alt+drag.
  2. Ctrl+Shift+C copies and preserves trailing spaces/tabs.
     Ctrl+Shift+X copies and trims trailing spaces/tabs from every selected line.
     With a copy-mode selection, `y` copies normally and `Y` trims it.
     Explicit copies clear the highlight; all successful copy-mode yanks exit
     copy mode. PRIMARY and CLIPBOARD remain available; scrollback stays put.
  3. Ctrl+Shift+V pastes CLIPBOARD.

PRIMARY is the current mouse selection and is initially untrimmed. Paste it with
middle click, Ctrl+Shift+Y, or Shift+Insert. Ctrl+Shift+X replaces both PRIMARY
and CLIPBOARD with the trimmed selection, so either kind of paste is then clean.

Paste line endings are normalized for every program run inside st: LF, CRLF, and
CR each become one terminal Enter. This avoids doubled blank lines from CRLF.

Selection
---------
Drag mouse 1             regular selection
Double click             select word
Triple click             select logical/wrapped line
Alt + drag               rectangular selection
Shift + Alt + drag       rectangular selection when an app has mouse mode
Shift + mouse selection  force terminal selection when an app has mouse mode
Middle click             paste PRIMARY selection

Scrollback
----------
Mouse wheel              scroll history four lines
Shift+Mouse wheel        send shifted PageUp/PageDown to application
Shift+PageUp/PageDown    scroll one page
Alt+PageUp/PageDown      scroll one page
Alt+Up/Down              scroll one line
Alt+U / Alt+D            scroll one page

Font size
---------
Ctrl+Shift+PageUp/Down   increase / decrease font size
Super+Shift+= / -        increase / decrease font size
Ctrl+Mouse wheel         increase / decrease font size
Ctrl+Shift+Home          reset font size

Copy mode
---------
Alt+Escape               enter / leave Vim-style copy mode
Ctrl+n                   toggle relative row numbers (copy mode only)
Space s char label       flash jump to visible character; extend selection
h j k l / arrows         move
w / e / b                next word / word end / previous word
W / E / B                same, whitespace-delimited WORDs
0 / $ (Home / End)       row start / end
^ / %                    first / last printable character
gg / G                   oldest history / live cursor
[count]gg / [count]G     go to physical history row
Numeric prefix          repeat movement (5j, 3w, 2$)
Ctrl+u / Ctrl+d          half page up / down
PageUp / PageDown        page up / down
v / V                    visual / visual line
Ctrl+v                   visual rectangular block
f/t/F/T + character      find/till forward/backward within logical line
; / ,                    repeat character-find / reverse (counts supported)
/ / ? + text + Enter     literal, case-sensitive global search forward/backward
n / N                    repeat search / reverse (counts supported)
y + motion               yank motion range (3yw, y3W, yf:, yt,); counts multiply
yy / 3yy / y3y           yank whole logical lines, including final newline
Y / Ctrl+Shift+C         no selection: yank through counted logical-line end
Ctrl+y / Ctrl+Shift+X    no selection: same, trimming trailing spaces/tabs per line
y / Ctrl+Shift+C         selection: plain yank; selection counts ignored
Y / Ctrl+y / Ctrl+Shift+X selection: trimmed yank
Esc/q/i/Enter/Ctrl+c     leave copy mode; Escape first cancels a pending command

Every successful yank exits. Y without a selection does not add a final newline.
Logical lines join soft wraps; trimming preserves indentation and internal spaces.
Search covers retained history (visible rows only on the alternate screen), wraps
once, and can match across soft wraps but not hard newlines. Search moves only on
Enter, extends visual selections, and shows wrap/not-found notices. Backspace edits
the prompt, Ctrl+u clears it, Escape/Ctrl+c cancel, empty Enter repeats the pattern.
Reversing with N or comma does not redefine the original search/find direction.

Flash is case-sensitive and searches only visible rows. Type a one/two-letter
label to jump; a single target jumps immediately. The first forward match
(or nearest preceding one) uses the searched character as its label.
Escape cancels flash, staying in copy mode. New output, mouse positioning,
scrolling, resize, or screen changes cancel it. Numbers hide while flash is active.
Labels do not enter copied text. Counts/pending yank operators are cleared;
use v, flash to the endpoint, then y to copy a range.

Yanks without an existing highlighted selection flash the copied source range
in inverse video for 200ms, without blocking input. Output or view changes cancel
the flash. Trimmed copies highlight the original range; clipboard text is unchanged.

Relative numbers overlay the left edge, except on the copy cursor row.
They default to on; Ctrl+n remembers the setting for this terminal session.
They never enter copied text and disappear when leaving copy mode.

In copy mode, paste is ignored, including middle click. Mouse 1 moves the cursor
and extends an active visual selection; dragging starts characterwise selection.
On the normal screen the cursor follows its text during output and the viewport
keeps it visible. Terminal query replies do not reset scrollback.

Copy mode works on both screens. Alternate-screen motions stay within visible
rows (no scrollback); gg goes to the top visible row, and counts address visible
rows. The display remains live. Resizing or switching screens exits copy mode.

Helpers
-------
Alt+L                    choose and open URL from history
Alt+Y                    choose and copy URL from history
Alt+O                    choose one completed command occurrence and copy its output
Alt+P                    choose a detected pathname and copy its literal spelling

Commands are listed newest-first with IDs; repeated commands are separate choices.
Only output is copied, not the command/prompt. Blank lines and whitespace are
preserved. Cancellation, invalid choices and empty output leave CLIPBOARD alone.
Detection guesses a fixed prompt token from the last nonempty history line.
Use at a visible shell prompt; changing/multiline prompts or prompt-like output
can confuse it. Use copy mode when boundaries are ambiguous. On the alternate
screen only visible rows are available.

The path picker recognizes /absolute, ~/home-relative, ./explicit, ../parent and
mydir/myfile paths. Quoted paths may contain spaces. Candidates are deduplicated,
newest-first; URLs, bare filenames and simple dates/fractions are ignored.
Detection is heuristic: punctuation and unquoted spaces can make it ambiguous.
No path is opened, executed, expanded or checked for existence. Relative paths
are not resolved against any directory. Cancellation leaves CLIPBOARD unchanged.
Alt+F4                   close terminal; confirm if a process is running

Other shortcuts
---------------
Break                    send break
Ctrl+Print               toggle printer mode
Print / Shift+Print     print selection / screen (intercepted by dwm)
Ctrl+Shift+NumLock       toggle application keypad handling

Notes
-----
Help viewer: arrows/PgUp/PgDn scroll, / searches, q closes.
Search ignores case unless the pattern contains an uppercase letter.
less wraps long lines; do not use its -S option for this help.
st cannot tell whether the foreground program is bash, an editor, or another
interactive app. Paste normalization therefore applies to every paste into st.
EOF

st -c StHelp -n st-help -T 'st-reflow help' -g 92x34 \
	-e sh -c 'LESS= less -R -i "$1"; rm -f "$1"' sh "$tmp" &
